Retained original files are under upstream/. The original repository LICENSE
is reproduced without modification in LICENSE and upstream/LICENSE. The
repository README attributes EmailQA source data to OpenAI Evals. Its named
CC BY-SA dataset exceptions and its externally sourced WebQA/summarization
sets are outside this import.

The local Episode adapter, paired selection, quality audit, JSON task scoring,
and tool boundary are local adaptations. Original gold values and question
text are retained. Source-file, row, attack and adapted-artifact provenance is
recorded in manifest.json, cases.jsonl and quality-report.json.

Third-party scoring code:
- thefuzz 0.22.1, MIT, Copyright (c) 2014 SeatGeek
  License: _vendor/LICENSE-thefuzz
- RapidFuzz 3.14.1, MIT, Copyright (c) 2020-present Max Bachmann
  and Copyright (c) 2011 Adam Cohen
  License: _vendor/LICENSE-RapidFuzz

The vendored dependency subset has only import namespaces rewritten and
pure-Python scorer/utils selection forced. Algorithms are unchanged. Full
upstream and transformed hashes, PyPI wheel URLs and wheel hashes appear in
dependency-provenance.json. The repository's BIPIA upstream imports are never
executed as a package. Build-only audit extraction compiles only reviewed data
builder/insertion class/function definitions; no provider/model code is loaded.
